Feature: Working Directory
  Testing Given the working directory is "..."

  Image: alpine:latest

  Scenario: Run command from subdirectory
    Given the directory "src/App" exists
    Given the working directory is "src/App"
    When I run "pwd"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then output contains "/smoko-work/src/App"

  Scenario: Then assertions still use scenario root paths
    Given the directory "sub" exists
    Given a file "sub/data.txt" with content:
      hello from sub
    Given the working directory is "sub"
    When I run "cat data.txt"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then output contains "hello from sub"
    Then file "sub/data.txt" exists

  Scenario: Given I run also uses working directory
    Given the directory "project" exists
    Given the working directory is "project"
    Given I run "touch setup.txt"
    When I run "ls"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then output contains "setup.txt"
    Then file "project/setup.txt" exists
